[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/semver_solver/tests/semver_solver_impl_test.py: Expanded contract coverage per feedback: (1) compare_precedence now asserts both directions of the numeric-below-alphanumeric prerelease ranking. (2) parse_range now covers the '>' comparator, caret zero-major (^0.2.3) and zero-minor/zero-major (^0.0.3) boundaries, wildcard operands combined with >, >=, <, <=, and !=, wildcard-only caret (^1.x) and tilde (~1.x) operands, hyphen ranges with wildcard endpoints (1.x - 2.x), and comparator operands carrying valid build metadata (>=1.0.0+build.1). (3) satisfies now exercises the '>' comparator, all caret/wildcard/hyphen/build-operand branches above, and include_prerelease=True precedence evaluation both inside a band (1.2.0-beta vs >=1.0.0 <2.0.0) and at an upper boundary (2.0.0-beta vs <2.0.0 vs include_prerelease False filtering). (4) resolve now covers the already-chosen-release conflict branch: bee 2.0.0 is chosen first (fewest candidates), app 2.0.0's 'bee 1.x' requirement conflicts with that assignment and is recorded, the branch is backtracked, and app 1.0.0 requiring bee >=2.0.0 is selected, asserting the final assignment. NOTE ON REMAINING FEEDBACK ITEMS: assertions on InvalidVersionError, InvalidRangeError, PackageNotFoundError, and ResolutionConflictError were implemented and then removed because the workspace checker rejects them with [NO_ERROR_TESTING]: 'Contract violation errors (*Error) designate checked preconditions that callers must satisfy and cannot be tested (found ...)'. That lint resolves even aliased imports, so no compliant way exists to assert these precondition errors in this workspace; the omission is mandated by the checker, not by a gap in coverage intent.
